\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks the branch. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4: the exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted), held until each grid's own truncation noise excites the unstable mode---level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the \emph  {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends; muted lines carry the last reading (the level-3 run continues to $t=100$ behind a trapped surface). (b)~The deviation is a single exponential mode with a level-dependent sign: plateau fits give $\tau =5.88$/$5.26$ at levels 3/4, i.e.\ $T=0.87$/$0.78$, within $15\%$ of the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach rate~\cite  {gonzalez2009}. (c)~Level 3 with the seed \emph  {declared}, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward. The fate is opposite to the push, the twins cross at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$, and a tenfold smaller kick arrives $11$--$12$ units later at matched horizon radius ($8$--$14$ across markers). Gold: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$; cross: death at $t=40.1$.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_throat}{{1}{5}{The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks the branch. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4: the exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted), held until each grid's own truncation noise excites the unstable mode---level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the \emph {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends; muted lines carry the last reading (the level-3 run continues to $t=100$ behind a trapped surface). (b)~The deviation is a single exponential mode with a level-dependent sign: plateau fits give $\tau =5.88$/$5.26$ at levels 3/4, i.e.\ $T=0.87$/$0.78$, within $15\%$ of the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach rate~\cite {gonzalez2009}. (c)~Level 3 with the seed \emph {declared}, Eq.~\eqref {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward. The fate is opposite to the push, the twins cross at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$, and a tenfold smaller kick arrives $11$--$12$ units later at matched horizon radius ($8$--$14$ across markers). Gold: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$; cross: death at $t=40.1$}{figure.1}{}}
