\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The inflation branch, fully instrumented ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$, level 4), the mirror of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_collapse}. (a)~Minimal-surface areal radius (ink) against the unkicked level-4 twin (grey), whose own truncation seed inflates it: $3.81\to 11.39$ ($\times 3.0$) against $\times 2.2$, the two parting by $10\%$ at $t=25$---the time by which the $+10^{-2}$ twin on this level has already formed its horizon. Gold: the scan rows carrying an anti-trapped shell, $\theta _+>0$ and $\theta _->0$, the marginally trapped surface's mirror, held from $t=1$ to $35$. (b)--(d)~Gauge and matter at the origin: $\min \alpha $ falls $0.214\to 0.080$, $\max |K|$ peaks at $0.057$ at $t=40.6$ and then decays, and $\min \chi $ \emph  {rises} $2.4\times 10^{-8}\to 1.4\times 10^{-3}$---the opposite of the collapse branch in every one. (e),(f)~Shell profiles to $r=4$, light $=$ early: the compactified inner sheet's $\chi $-trough marches outward, $r=0.016\to 2.9$. That march is what the flickering $\theta _+=0$ rows at $R\approx 61$ after $t=85$ are---the far universe's image crossing the scan window---and not a horizon. (g)~Constraints hold to $t\simeq 50$ and then grow, $60\times $ in $\mathcal  {H}$ by $t=100$; the record is quoted only where the mode is exponential.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_inflation}{{3}{8}{The inflation branch, fully instrumented ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$, level 4), the mirror of Fig.~\ref {fig:single_collapse}. (a)~Minimal-surface areal radius (ink) against the unkicked level-4 twin (grey), whose own truncation seed inflates it: $3.81\to 11.39$ ($\times 3.0$) against $\times 2.2$, the two parting by $10\%$ at $t=25$---the time by which the $+10^{-2}$ twin on this level has already formed its horizon. Gold: the scan rows carrying an anti-trapped shell, $\theta _+>0$ and $\theta _->0$, the marginally trapped surface's mirror, held from $t=1$ to $35$. (b)--(d)~Gauge and matter at the origin: $\min \alpha $ falls $0.214\to 0.080$, $\max |K|$ peaks at $0.057$ at $t=40.6$ and then decays, and $\min \chi $ \emph {rises} $2.4\times 10^{-8}\to 1.4\times 10^{-3}$---the opposite of the collapse branch in every one. (e),(f)~Shell profiles to $r=4$, light $=$ early: the compactified inner sheet's $\chi $-trough marches outward, $r=0.016\to 2.9$. That march is what the flickering $\theta _+=0$ rows at $R\approx 61$ after $t=85$ are---the far universe's image crossing the scan window---and not a horizon. (g)~Constraints hold to $t\simeq 50$ and then grow, $60\times $ in $\mathcal {H}$ by $t=100$; the record is quoted only where the mode is exponential}{figure.3}{}}
