\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The head-on merger makes a black hole ($d=8$ from rest, opposite scalar signs), on the seamless arm: maximum level $5$ from $t=0$, no restart, no mesh seam, no interior device, $t=0\to 100$ with no NaN. It supersedes the level-3$\to $5 chain of earlier drafts, which it reproduces (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wall}). Every horizon point is the orientation-corrected scan; the level-3 scout is kept only to mark its wall. (a)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits from $d=7.94$ (the tracker's grid snap on a true $8$): the common MOTS forms at $t=22$ (gold rule in every time panel), the scout dies at the level-3 wall at $t=26.91$ (dashed rule), and one merged pit runs on to $t=100$. (b)~The minimum lapse rides the $10^{-10}$ clamp over $t=38.2$--$41.5$ and settles at $1.4\times 10^{-3}$. (c)~Minimum $\chi $: excursions onto the $10^{-20}$ clamp leave the frame from $t=30.6$; the arm returns and settles at $2.0\times 10^{-5}$. (d)~The wall is resolution: $\max |K|$ blows up to $18.1$ at the level-3 death; level 5 peaks at $1.36$ and ends at $0.13$. (e)~The scout's $\|\mathcal  {H}\|$ explodes at the wall ($13.6$); the seamless arm's norms \emph  {fall} the whole way, $4.8\times 10^{-3}\to 2.7\times 10^{-3}$. The down-step arm (level 3, restarted from the seamed chain's $t=35$ checkpoint) sits a constant ${\sim }0.2$~dex below in $\|\mathcal  {H}\|$---a coarser grid's own truncation---while tracking the same horizon mass to $1.3\%$. (f)~The horizon: filled diamonds, offline scans at $\mathrm  {d}x=0.0625$ (formation at $t=22$, $r=3.17$, $R=5.56$; growth to $5.71$ by $t=24$; then $4.72$, and $4.92/4.87$ at $t=42.5/43$); open circles, the live scan on three arms. Its gaps are aperture, not horizon loss---the shells reach $0.5\,d+2.3$, so once the pits merge the surface at $r\simeq 2.7$--$3.3$ lies outside while every shell within reports trapped; where two arms see it at once they agree ($t=36$: $R=4.456$ against $4.441$). The dashed line is a straight-line fit to the tracked radius, $-0.00658$ per unit (r.m.s.\ $0.032$); an exponential does not converge on this record, so no asymptotic radius is resolvable. (g)~The Misner--Sharp mass falls, $2.99$ at formation to $2.17$ at $t=99$---phantom infall \emph  {removes} mass---but it does not fall without end. The dashed curve is $M_\infty +b\,e^{-(t-36)/\tau }$ fitted on the tracked points: $M_\infty =2.160\pm 0.006$, $\tau =19.4\pm 0.8$ (r.m.s.\ $0.011$, a factor $4.8$ better than the straight line, dotted asymptote). The remnant is settling to a finite mass, and on the same clock as the scalar channel's shut-off, $\tau =19$--$28$ (Fig.~\ref {fig:scalar_censorship}). (h)~Expansions at the areal minimum: $\theta _+$ crosses zero between $t=20$ and $21$, both negative by $t=24$; the per-mouth scans never find an own MOTS---the horizon is born common. (i)~The field's extrema fall $\pm 0.90\to \pm 0.008$ with $|\Pi |\le 0.07$: the supporting scalar is swallowed and radiated, leaving vacuum around a black hole. (j)~The remnant's $(2,0)$ mode at $R=10$, peak $r\psi _4=+2.33\times 10^{-2}$ at $t=28.2$, rings with period ${\sim }31$--$39$, $\times 0.6$--$0.8$ per half-swing, as the mass in (g) settles; the same number and the same convention as Sec.~\ref {sec:gw} and Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}.}}{10}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headon_collapse}{{5}{10}{The head-on merger makes a black hole ($d=8$ from rest, opposite scalar signs), on the seamless arm: maximum level $5$ from $t=0$, no restart, no mesh seam, no interior device, $t=0\to 100$ with no NaN. It supersedes the level-3$\to $5 chain of earlier drafts, which it reproduces (Sec.~\ref {sec:headon:wall}). Every horizon point is the orientation-corrected scan; the level-3 scout is kept only to mark its wall. (a)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits from $d=7.94$ (the tracker's grid snap on a true $8$): the common MOTS forms at $t=22$ (gold rule in every time panel), the scout dies at the level-3 wall at $t=26.91$ (dashed rule), and one merged pit runs on to $t=100$. (b)~The minimum lapse rides the $10^{-10}$ clamp over $t=38.2$--$41.5$ and settles at $1.4\times 10^{-3}$. (c)~Minimum $\chi $: excursions onto the $10^{-20}$ clamp leave the frame from $t=30.6$; the arm returns and settles at $2.0\times 10^{-5}$. (d)~The wall is resolution: $\max |K|$ blows up to $18.1$ at the level-3 death; level 5 peaks at $1.36$ and ends at $0.13$. (e)~The scout's $\|\mathcal {H}\|$ explodes at the wall ($13.6$); the seamless arm's norms \emph {fall} the whole way, $4.8\times 10^{-3}\to 2.7\times 10^{-3}$. The down-step arm (level 3, restarted from the seamed chain's $t=35$ checkpoint) sits a constant ${\sim }0.2$~dex below in $\|\mathcal {H}\|$---a coarser grid's own truncation---while tracking the same horizon mass to $1.3\%$. (f)~The horizon: filled diamonds, offline scans at $\mathrm {d}x=0.0625$ (formation at $t=22$, $r=3.17$, $R=5.56$; growth to $5.71$ by $t=24$; then $4.72$, and $4.92/4.87$ at $t=42.5/43$); open circles, the live scan on three arms. Its gaps are aperture, not horizon loss---the shells reach $0.5\,d+2.3$, so once the pits merge the surface at $r\simeq 2.7$--$3.3$ lies outside while every shell within reports trapped; where two arms see it at once they agree ($t=36$: $R=4.456$ against $4.441$). The dashed line is a straight-line fit to the tracked radius, $-0.00658$ per unit (r.m.s.\ $0.032$); an exponential does not converge on this record, so no asymptotic radius is resolvable. (g)~The Misner--Sharp mass falls, $2.99$ at formation to $2.17$ at $t=99$---phantom infall \emph {removes} mass---but it does not fall without end. The dashed curve is $M_\infty +b\,e^{-(t-36)/\tau }$ fitted on the tracked points: $M_\infty =2.160\pm 0.006$, $\tau =19.4\pm 0.8$ (r.m.s.\ $0.011$, a factor $4.8$ better than the straight line, dotted asymptote). The remnant is settling to a finite mass, and on the same clock as the scalar channel's shut-off, $\tau =19$--$28$ (Fig.~\ref {fig:scalar_censorship}). (h)~Expansions at the areal minimum: $\theta _+$ crosses zero between $t=20$ and $21$, both negative by $t=24$; the per-mouth scans never find an own MOTS---the horizon is born common. (i)~The field's extrema fall $\pm 0.90\to \pm 0.008$ with $|\Pi |\le 0.07$: the supporting scalar is swallowed and radiated, leaving vacuum around a black hole. (j)~The remnant's $(2,0)$ mode at $R=10$, peak $r\psi _4=+2.33\times 10^{-2}$ at $t=28.2$, rings with period ${\sim }31$--$39$, $\times 0.6$--$0.8$ per half-swing, as the mass in (g) settles; the same number and the same convention as Sec.~\ref {sec:gw} and Fig.~\ref {fig:gw_gallery}}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The merging binary's mouths, measured. Both arms start at $d=12$ with the same throats and differ in tangential momentum, $p=0.12$ against $0.45$; they also differ in grid, the merger's instrumented re-run carrying three refinement levels against the fly-by's five, so the shared $\tau $ below is a result across two resolutions rather than a controlled one-knob comparison. (a)~Areal radius of one mouth, its twin tracking it to $2\times 10^{-4}$: solid while the two oriented scan spheres are disjoint, dotted once they overlap and the reading is a property of the pair; long dash, the common-centre scan enclosing both. No marginally trapped surface forms in either arm. (b)~Separation: $p=0.12$ reaches contact, $p=0.45$ misses at $4.8$. (c)~Growth excess $R_{\rm  areal}/R_0-1$ with exponential fits over $t=8$--$25$ (gold), $\tau =3.70$ for the merger against $4.39$ for the fly-by---the arm that merges inflates on the clock of the arm that misses.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mouth_growth}{{6}{11}{The merging binary's mouths, measured. Both arms start at $d=12$ with the same throats and differ in tangential momentum, $p=0.12$ against $0.45$; they also differ in grid, the merger's instrumented re-run carrying three refinement levels against the fly-by's five, so the shared $\tau $ below is a result across two resolutions rather than a controlled one-knob comparison. (a)~Areal radius of one mouth, its twin tracking it to $2\times 10^{-4}$: solid while the two oriented scan spheres are disjoint, dotted once they overlap and the reading is a property of the pair; long dash, the common-centre scan enclosing both. No marginally trapped surface forms in either arm. (b)~Separation: $p=0.12$ reaches contact, $p=0.45$ misses at $4.8$. (c)~Growth excess $R_{\rm areal}/R_0-1$ with exponential fits over $t=8$--$25$ (gold), $\tau =3.70$ for the merger against $4.39$ for the fly-by---the arm that merges inflates on the clock of the arm that misses}{figure.6}{}}
