0.15$---the gauge collapse and the curvature wall are different places}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The wall does not move: death time of the $p=0.12$ spiral against refinement, every arm restarted from the same $t=50$ checkpoint, every death an $h_{11}$ NaN, no horizon at any rung. Filled: plain evolution, per-doubling gains marked. Open diamond: the level-5 arm at half the time step. Open circles: the core-damping family---a different treatment, dying on the same clock. Faint rule: the production chain (doubled base grid, restart at $t=36$), $4.2$ units past the whole ladder and still short of the merger's end.}}{13}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
