\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Every source on a detector at one shared calibration: total mass $M=30\,M_\odot $, distance $D=10$ Mpc, each record first reduced to units of its own total ADM mass; strain scales as $M/D$, frequency as $1/M$. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere on a common merger clock ($\tau =0$ at each peak): fly-by loudest ($8.2\times 10^{-2}$), then spiral, head-on, vacuum twin, lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each curve drawn from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked), below which a record of length $T$ cannot tell a wave from a drift. Read them as falling power laws (slopes $-3.3$ to $-5.9$) with no resolved maximum: any ``peak'' taken from this panel is the corner $1/T$; the values at the resolved $\Psi _4$ peaks are quoted in the text. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde  h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz---the ramp an astrophysical binary rides into the band where the simulated signal begins. (c)~Instantaneous frequency over each record's body against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$, the textbook merger value; no wormhole channel does (tracks in Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole, ranked; the tick on each bar is the spread over extraction spheres, the error bar that catches near-zone content posing as a wave (fly-by $43\%$, the widest: the expansion of its open mouths is near-zone content the outer spheres see less of). Open gold bars: the published equal-mass vacuum results from rest at infinity---head-on infall $5.5\times 10^{-4}$, quasi-circular merger $4.84\times 10^{-2}$---which bracket any \emph  {vacuum} binary and need not bracket a ghost one; the spiral and fly-by outradiate the vacuum merger control by $8.5\times $ and $29\times $. That control carries the spiral's momentum; against the momentum-matched vacuum pass of Sec.~\ref {sec:gw} the fly-by's factor is ${\simeq }70$. Energies are band integrals of $|\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\Psi _4\,\mathrm  {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for the $\pm m$ pair; gravitational channel only---the scalar's own energy is invisible to $\Psi _4$ and is measured separately in Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}, where it is larger than every bar here and of the opposite sign.}}{15}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_ligo}{{10}{15}{Every source on a detector at one shared calibration: total mass $M=30\,M_\odot $, distance $D=10$ Mpc, each record first reduced to units of its own total ADM mass; strain scales as $M/D$, frequency as $1/M$. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere on a common merger clock ($\tau =0$ at each peak): fly-by loudest ($8.2\times 10^{-2}$), then spiral, head-on, vacuum twin, lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (gold), each curve drawn from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked), below which a record of length $T$ cannot tell a wave from a drift. Read them as falling power laws (slopes $-3.3$ to $-5.9$) with no resolved maximum: any ``peak'' taken from this panel is the corner $1/T$; the values at the resolved $\Psi _4$ peaks are quoted in the text. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz---the ramp an astrophysical binary rides into the band where the simulated signal begins. (c)~Instantaneous frequency over each record's body against the point-mass chirp (gold), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$, the textbook merger value; no wormhole channel does (tracks in Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole, ranked; the tick on each bar is the spread over extraction spheres, the error bar that catches near-zone content posing as a wave (fly-by $43\%$, the widest: the expansion of its open mouths is near-zone content the outer spheres see less of). Open gold bars: the published equal-mass vacuum results from rest at infinity---head-on infall $5.5\times 10^{-4}$, quasi-circular merger $4.84\times 10^{-2}$---which bracket any \emph {vacuum} binary and need not bracket a ghost one; the spiral and fly-by outradiate the vacuum merger control by $8.5\times $ and $29\times $. That control carries the spiral's momentum; against the momentum-matched vacuum pass of Sec.~\ref {sec:gw} the fly-by's factor is ${\simeq }70$. Energies are band integrals of $|\int r\Psi _4\,\mathrm {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for the $\pm m$ pair; gravitational channel only---the scalar's own energy is invisible to $\Psi _4$ and is measured separately in Sec.~\ref {sec:gw:scalar}, where it is larger than every bar here and of the opposite sign}{figure.10}{}}
