\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces One throat's wave is linear in its deformation. (a)~$\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4^{2,0}$ at $R=14$, each arm divided by its own seed: $\varepsilon _2=0.005$, $0.01$, $0.05$ and the kick-free $0.01$ arm collapse onto one curve. (b)~rms amplitude over $t=30$--$50$ against $\varepsilon _2$ at three spheres, with the slope-one line through the $0.01$ arm: linear to $1$--$16\%$ across a decade. The open circle is the pure quadrupole---no radial kick---matching the kicked arm to $2$--$3\%$; the dashed rule is the spherical control's floor.}}{16}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seed_linearity}{{11}{16}{One throat's wave is linear in its deformation. (a)~$\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4^{2,0}$ at $R=14$, each arm divided by its own seed: $\varepsilon _2=0.005$, $0.01$, $0.05$ and the kick-free $0.01$ arm collapse onto one curve. (b)~rms amplitude over $t=30$--$50$ against $\varepsilon _2$ at three spheres, with the slope-one line through the $0.01$ arm: linear to $1$--$16\%$ across a decade. The open circle is the pure quadrupole---no radial kick---matching the kicked arm to $2$--$3\%$; the dashed rule is the spherical control's floor}{figure.11}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Moving the fill window does not move the wave. (a)~$r\,\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4^{2,2}$ at $R=20$ for the freeze arm (fill $1.40/1.90$, ink) and its twin ($1.25/1.75$, gold dots), same $t=57$ checkpoint, same binary: one bicolour curve. (b)~The per-sphere envelope of the difference against the few-percent gate: at most $0.385\%$ of peak at $R=20$ and $0.013\%$ at $R=44$, each front arriving on the fill's causal clock $t=57+(R-1.9)$. The figure certifies the fill's inertness, not a remnant ringdown.}}{16}{figure.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fill_insensitivity}{{12}{16}{Moving the fill window does not move the wave. (a)~$r\,\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4^{2,2}$ at $R=20$ for the freeze arm (fill $1.40/1.90$, ink) and its twin ($1.25/1.75$, gold dots), same $t=57$ checkpoint, same binary: one bicolour curve. (b)~The per-sphere envelope of the difference against the few-percent gate: at most $0.385\%$ of peak at $R=20$ and $0.013\%$ at $R=44$, each front arriving on the fill's causal clock $t=57+(R-1.9)$. The figure certifies the fill's inertness, not a remnant ringdown}{figure.12}{}}
